# Force LF line endings for every text file regardless of host OS.
#
# Without this, git's default `core.autocrlf=true` on Windows converts
# LF → CRLF on checkout. The on-disk byte content then differs between
# platforms, which broke `crates/source-hash/`'s freshness check on
# v0.8.7-rc{1,2}: same logical sources hashed to different SHA-256 on
# the Linux producer vs. the Windows consumer of the wasm bundle.
# Forcing LF everywhere makes file bytes platform-invariant, which is
# what every cross-platform reproducibility check assumes.
#
# Binary files are auto-detected by `text=auto` and not converted.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Renormalize on next `git add --renormalize .`; existing commits are
# unaffected (the LF-on-disk → LF-in-objects identity holds since the
# repo was committed from Linux/macOS contributors). Windows
# contributors: re-checkout (`git checkout-index --force --all`) or
# clone fresh after pulling this file.
